For a harmonic oscillator $m \ddot{x} + c \dot{x} + k x = 0$ with $m = 12.5\text{ kg}$ and $k = 135.0\text{ N/m}$, critical damping occurs when the discriminant $c^2 - 4mk = 0$:
$$c_{\text{crit}} = 2\sqrt{m k} = 2\sqrt{12.5 \times 135.0} \approx 82.158\text{ N\cdot s/m}$$
Semi-implicit Euler step for camera displacement $x$ and velocity $v$ over $\Delta t$:
```cpp
float Accel = (-135.0f * Displacement - 82.158f * Velocity) / 12.5f;
Velocity += Accel * DeltaTime;
Displacement += Velocity * DeltaTime;
```

